          "title": "Exploring Million.js with Aiden Bai",
          "duration": "4:58:30",
          "channel": "Ryan Carniato",
          "description": "In this stream Million.js creator, Aiden Bai, joins us to talk about the latest performance improvements Virtual DOM-land, the Block VDOM. How is it so fast? Is it enough to change the way we look at Virtual DOMs? Maybe VDOMs aren't pure overhead afterall?\n\n[0:00] Preamble\n[13:45] Introducing Aiden Bai\n[19:00] Aiden's Early Work\n[24:30] Discovering Block VDOM / Early Benchmarks\n[36:00] Looking Closely at the Benchmarks \n[54:00] Back in Block - How Does Million.js Work?\n[1:11:00] Million.js Without React\n[1:24:30] Q&A: Vue? Vercel? React Benchmark? For Component?\n[1:30:15] Understanding The Compiler with Pseudo-Code\n[1:42:15] Q&A: React Performance? Solid?\n[1:48:15] Stonks Example \n[1:55:00] React Fiber Example\n[2:08:00] Authoring Experience and Custom Components\n[2:24:00] Q&A: Sponsorship? Future Plans? Hair?\n[2:33:00] Aiden's Parting Notes & Intermission\n[2:39:15] This Week in JavaScript: Chrome Sponsors Solid!\n[2:51:00] TWiJ: Q & A about Google Sponsorship\n[3:03:00] TWiJ: New Solid Logo\n[3:07:45] TWiJ: Netlify Lay-offs\n[3:19:00] TWiJ: Dan Jutan\n[3:56:15] TWiJ: Prisma 5.0\n[4:05:00] Angular, Nitro, and Analog\n[4:09:00] Q&A: Blazor? SolidStart? But seriously, Blazor?\n[4:31:00] Q&A: Marko? Remix? Cache API? New JS Proposals?\n[4:47:00] Conclusion - Solid 2.0, Async Signals, and More on Caches\n\nThank you @zombiefacesupreme for the timestamps!",
